# Generated from the OSRS Wiki page "Transcript:Hazeel Cult" by tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py
# Hand-fixed after generation: added the condition headers the poison-after-full-inventory and amulet branches lacked.
0	section	Starting off
1	line	Player	Hello there.
1	line	Ceril Carnillean	Blooming, thieving cultists! Why don't they leave me alone? String them all up, that's what I say!
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	What's wrong?
2	line	Player	What's wrong?
2	line	Ceril Carnillean	It's those blooming cultists from the south! They keep breaking into my house!
2	line	Player	Have they taken much?
2	line	Ceril Carnillean	Well... no. They stole a suit of armour when they first broke in months ago, but they've been back four more times since then and taken nothing.
2	line	Player	I see. And you are?
2	line	Ceril Carnillean	You don't know me? Why, I am Sir Ceril Carnillean! Mine is quite a famous bloodline, you know. We've played a vital role in the politics of Ardougne for many generations.
2	line	Player	Well I'm {player}. Maybe I can help you with these cultists?
2	line	Ceril Carnillean	Interesting... I suppose the authorities haven't been much help so far. Yes, very well. If you return the stolen armour, I will provide you with a modest cash reward!
2	action	If the player is below level 10 combat:
3	box	Before starting this quest, be aware that your combat level is lower than the recommended level of 10.
2	select	Start the Hazeel Cult quest?
2	option	Yes.
3	line	Player	Yes, of course, I'd be happy to help.
3	line	Ceril Carnillean	That's very noble of you! Keep that attitude up and one day you might have the honour of working full-time for someone like me.
3	line	Ceril Carnillean	Now, I caught a glimpse of the thieves leaving, but due to... uh... my cold, I was unable to give chase.
3	line	Ceril Carnillean	What I do know is that they belong to some sort of cult. They seem to be based in a cave just south of the city, near the Clock Tower.
3	line	Player	How do you know that?
3	line	Ceril Carnillean	My old butler, Higson, once followed them there. Unfortunately, the next night he died in his sleep.
3	line	Player	That's awful!
3	line	Ceril Carnillean	No, it's okay. Jones, a replacement from the Servants' Guild, arrived the next day. He's been great - makes an excellent broth!
3	line	Player	Right... I'll see if I can find this cave.
3	action	end
2	option	No.
3	line	Player	No thanks. I've got other plans.
3	line	Ceril Carnillean	Well no wonder I'm the one with the big house and you're the one on the streets.
3	action	end
1	option	You probably deserve it.
2	line	Player	You probably deserve it.
2	line	Ceril Carnillean	And who are you to judge me? You look like a peasant anyway. I'm wasting my time talking to you.
2	action	end
1	option	You seem uptight, I'll leave you alone.
2	line	Player	You seem uptight. I'll leave you alone.
2	line	Ceril Carnillean	Yes, I doubt you could help anyway.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Ceril again
1	line	Player	Hello, Ceril.
1	line	Ceril Carnillean	That's Sir Ceril to you, you impudent scamp. Show a bit of respect to your betters. Now, shouldn't you be recovering my armour?
1	line	Player	Yeah yeah, I'm on it.
1	line	Ceril Carnillean	Good. I suggest you start with that cave south of the city, near the Clock Tower. That is where the cult is based.
1	action	end
