0	section	Confronting the Hazeel Cult
1	line	Player	Hello there. Who are you?
1	line	Clivet	You can call me Clivet. What do you want, adventurer?
1	line	Player	Do you know the Carnilleans?
1	line	Clivet	Carnilleans? Don't think I've ever heard of them.
1	line	Player	Look, I know you're lying. I know all about your cult.
1	line	Clivet	Is that so? In that case, I'd say you'd be wise to leave now.
1	line	Player	Unfortunately, I have a job to do. I'm not leaving until it's done.
1	line	Clivet	Ah, I see. That two-faced snob has made you fall for his propaganda, eh?
1	line	Player	What's that supposed to mean?
1	line	Clivet	The Carnillean home does not belong to them. It was built long ago by the great Lord Hazeel, who once ruled over this entire region.
1	line	Clivet	Many years ago, the Carnilleans led a rebellion against Lord Hazeel and all who followed him. Under the cover of darkness, they stormed his home in an angry mob, torturing and butchering everyone they found.
1	line	Clivet	The following morning, the Carnillean forefathers moved into the empty household and claimed it as their own. They have grown fat on the hard work of Lord Hazeel ever since.
1	line	Player	Right... And what happened to this Hazeel?
1	line	Clivet	The foolish Carnilleans believed him dead. Unluckily for them, being an all-powerful Mahjarrat gave him access to powers and enchantments they knew nothing of.
1	line	Clivet	As they stormed his home, Lord Hazeel made preparations for his eventual return. We, his faithful followers, have been working to bring that about ever since.
1	line	Player	What makes you think I care about the politics and histories of Ardougne?
1	line	Clivet	I could kill you right now and be done with it, but I don't think you're the fool that the Carnilleans believe you to be. Instead, I offer you a chance to join us.
1	line	Clivet	Help us bring about the return of Lord Hazeel, and you will be well rewarded. However, should you continue to try and prevent his return, you will suffer the wrath of Zamorak.
1	line	Player	Hmm...
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	Before I decide, I have some questions for you.
2	line	Player	Before I decide, I have some questions for you.
2	line	Clivet	Very well.
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	Tell me more about Hazeel.
3	line	Player	Tell me more about Hazeel.
3	line	Clivet	Lord Hazeel is one of the great Mahjarrat who once fought alongside Zamorak himself. He ruled this region for many years, until the cowardly Carnilleans rebelled against him.
3	line	Player	But he survived?
3	line	Clivet	Of course! The Mahjarrat know magic that others can only dream of. Lord Hazeel used his abilities to ensure that one day he'd eventually return. That day will soon be upon us.
3	action	other
2	option	Why did the Carnilleans rebel against Hazeel?
3	line	Player	Why did the Carnilleans rebel against Hazeel?
3	line	Clivet	The Carnilleans served the pathetic Saradomin. They considered it their duty to overthrow Hazeel due to his loyalties to Zamorak. They were fools, blinded by Saradominist propaganda!
3	line	Player	Saradominist propaganda?
3	line	Clivet	Yes! Something even more prevalent today. Too many people now are fooled into believing that Saradomin is a god of good, while Zamorak is evil. Those lies couldn't be further from the truth!
3	action	other
2	option	Why do you keep breaking into the Carnillean Mansion?
3	line	Player	Why do you keep breaking into the Carnillean Mansion?
3	line	Clivet	There is something we need inside. I will say no more unless you agree to join us.
3	action	other
2	option	What can you tell me about the Mahjarrat?
3	line	Player	What can you tell me about the Mahjarrat?
3	line	Clivet	Surely you have heard of the Mahjarrat? Their race is the ultimate example of power! Each of them wields the strength of an entire army. To oppose any one of them, is to face your doom!
3	line	Player	And Hazeel is one of them?
3	line	Clivet	More than that! Hazeel is one of the greatest Mahjarrat to have ever lived!
3	line	Player	I see.
3	action	other
2	option	Actually, I have no questions.
3	line	Player	I have no more questions.
3	line	Clivet	Then we have nothing more to discuss until you've made your choice.
3	action	previous
1	option	Alright, I've made my decision.
2	line	Player	Alright, I've made my decision.
2	line	Clivet	And?
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	I'll help you.
3	line	Player	I'll help you.
3	line	Clivet	Good. Now, we are not the monsters that the Carnilleans would claim we are, so we were hoping to do this without violence. However, the fact they sent you here makes it clear that won't work now.
3	line	Player	Meaning?
3	line	Clivet	You must prove your loyalty to our cause, and Ceril Carnillean must die. Kill him for us, and we will know you are truly dedicated to Lord Hazeel.
3	select	Select an Option
3	option	Alright, how do I do it?
4	line	Player	Alright, how do I do it?
4	line	Clivet	I can already tell I was right about you. I can see you are of exactly the right character to join the followers of Hazeel.
4	line	Clivet	Here, take this poison and pour it into Ceril Carnillean's food. Once the deed is done, return here and speak to me once more.
4	action	If the player has a full inventory:
5	box	Clivet tries to give you some poison, but you don't have enough room to take it.
5	action	end
4	action	If the player inventory space:
5	box	Clivet gives you some poison.
5	action	end
3	option	I need some time to think on this.
4	line	Player	I need some time to think on this.
4	line	Clivet	Don't take too long.
4	action	end
2	option	I won't help you.
3	line	Player	I won't help you.
3	line	Clivet	Then you are a fool. Go back to your small-minded little life. You will never know the glories you could have tasted as one of us!
3	line	Player	You know I'm going to stop you, right?
3	line	Clivet	You'll try, but you'll never find us.
3	box	Clivet jumps onto the nearby raft and pushes off into the sewer system.
2	option	Actually, I need more time to think on this.
3	line	Player	Actually, I need more time to think on this.
3	line	Clivet	Don't take too long.
3	action	end
1	option	I need some time to think on this.
2	line	Player	I need some time to think on this.
2	line	Clivet	Don't take too long.
2	action	end
