0	section	Talking to the Guard
1	line	Player	Hello there.
1	line	Guard	Hello, adventurer. I hear you accused Jones of being part of that cult. Is that true?
1	line	Player	It is, but nobody believes me.
1	line	Guard	You have my utter faith, adventurer. I can't openly defy Sir Ceril, but I'd like you to know that I think you're on the right track with this.
1	line	Guard	I always found it suspicious that Jones would just show up on the doorstep the very day after the old butler died. Good luck in clearing your name
0	section	Accusing the butler
1	box	You search the cupboard and find a bottle of poison along with a mysterious amulet.
1	line	Player	And what do we have here...
1	line	Player	Ceril!
1	line	Ceril Carnillean	What do you want now you scoundrel?
1	line	Player	Take a look at what I've found.
1	line	Ceril Carnillean	What's this... Poison?
1	line	Ceril Carnillean	Jones?
1	line	Butler Jones	Just for killing rats, sir.
1	line	Ceril Carnillean	Right... but this amulet... I recognise this! Those cultists wore amulets like this!
1	line	Ceril Carnillean	Jones! We trusted you! We took you into our home!
1	line	Butler Jones	You senile old fool... it was all too easy! I should have killed you and your pathetic family weeks ago!
1	line	Ceril Carnillean	Guard!
1	line	Ceril Carnillean	This man is one of those cultists! Take him away!
1	line	Butler Jones	Don't think this is over, Ceril! You will die at the hands of the Hazeel Cult! I promise you that!
1	line	Ceril Carnillean	Well... It looks like I am indebted to you!
1	line	Player	No problem. We all make mistakes.
1	line	Ceril Carnillean	But if it weren't for you... my whole family... we could have been...
1	line	Ceril Carnillean	I apologise for my harshness before. The very least I can do is to reward you for your noble efforts, and to offer my sincerest apologies as a gentleman.
1	line	Player	Thank you.
1	line	Ceril Carnillean	No, no, thank you! Feel free to stop by anytime, adventurer!
