0	section	Talking to a Hazeel cultist
1	line	Player	Hello.
1	line	Hazeel Cultist	I cannot talk right now. Lord Hazeel will soon be back with us and I have many preparations to make.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Alomone
1	line	Player	Hello there.
1	line	Alomone	Well, well, well... we have a new recruit. Clivet told me of your desire to join us in our glorious task to resurrect the mighty Hazeel.
1	line	Player	That's right.
1	line	Alomone	Well if all goes well, you'll play a key role in just that. Before his defeat, Hazeel secured within his home a powerful magical scroll of restoration. It remains there still, hidden to even the foolish Carnilleans.
1	line	Alomone	Up to now, our attempts to recover this scroll have been met with disappointment. However, I know you will not fail us.
1	line	Player	So you want me to find this scroll?
1	line	Alomone	That is correct. You must return to the Carnillean Mansion and find where it is hidden. We already have an agent in place to support you.
1	line	Player	You do?
1	line	Alomone	Indeed. Their Butler Jones is in fact a faithful follower of Hazeel. He has been unsuccessful in locating the scroll himself, but together the two of you will find it.
1	line	Alomone	Now, go with haste. Soon we will restore Hazeel to his true power and glory!
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Alomone again
1	line	Player	Hello, Alomone.
1	line	Alomone	Hazeel has already waited far too long for his return. It is imperative that you find that scroll! It hides somewhere within the Carnillean Mansion.
1	line	Player	Don't worry, I'm on it.
1	action	end
0	section	Taking the raft back
1	box	The raft flows back to the cave entrance.
0	section	Talking to Clivet again
1	line	Player	Hello.
1	line	Clivet	It is good to see you once more, adventurer. Glory to Hazeel!
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Ceril again
1	line	Player	Hello, Ceril. How's things?
1	line	Ceril Carnillean	Sir Ceril! Sir! And things are terrible! Our beloved dog is dead, and I fear it's only a matter of time before those cultists strike again!
1	line	Player	Don't worry, I'm sure it will all be okay in the end.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Claus again
1	line	Player	Hello there.
1	line	Claus the Chef	I just don't understand it! How? How could someone poison my delicious food without me even noticing? I... I just don't get it!
1	line	Claus the Chef	Oh man... I hope I don't lose my job over this... but how? How did they do it? And why would they want to kill poor Scruffy anyway? He was such a good dog...
1	line	Player	Yeah... it's a real mystery.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Ceril
1	line	Player	Ceril. How are you?
1	line	Ceril Carnillean	Oh cruel world! Scruffy... I knew you well... I... just... don't think I can... go on without...
1	box	Sir Ceril breaks down into tears.
1	line	Player	Loosen up already. It was only a DOG.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Butler Jones
1	line	Player	Hello there.
1	line	Butler Jones	Hello, adventurer. I hear your quest is going well.
1	line	Player	I'm making progress. On that note, I hear you might be able to help me with my next task.
1	line	Butler Jones	Ah yes, the scroll. I'm afraid I've searched high and low, but have so far been unable to locate it. I'm sure it is somewhere within the house, hidden where even the family won't find it.
1	line	Player	Hmm... So it must be somewhere they'd have never stepped foot. I'll keep on looking.
1	action	end
